f an unconstrained inverse problem.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "A GPU-assisted physics-informed reconstruction framework fits spatial magnetization to measured field maps.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/magnetism/inverse-nv.html", "sha256": "90cfa855ce6679a0d5d58bfe4e2f5245318a374da83c3a73e4b3f8cfd3bbdcc4", "retrievedAt": "2026-11-25T06:26:11.240215+00:00", "doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2411.18882", "domain": "magnetism", "recordKind": "preprint", "sourceKind": "preprint"}</data></node><node id="mag-src-sot"><data key="title">[2512.23397] Terahertz switching of antiferromagnetic order by Néel spin-orbit torques</data><data key="kind">source</data><data key="domain">magnetism</data><data key="status">abstract-only</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "mag-src-sot", "title": "[2512.23397] Terahertz switching of antiferromagnetic order by Néel spin-orbit torques", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.23397", "authors": ["Behovits, Yannic", "Chekhov, Alexander L.", "Ruge, Amon", "Rouzegar, Reza", "Serrano, Bruno Rosinus", "Fellows, Alexander P.", "John, Ben", "Thämer, Martin", "Reimers, Sonka", "Renner, Fynn", "Dannegger, Tobias", "Nowak, Ulrich", "Seifert, Tom S.", "Kläui, Mathias", "Jourdan, Martin", "Kampfrath, Tobias"], "year": 2025, "version": "arXiv:2512.23397v1", "kind": "source", "status": "abstract-only", "readDepth": "abstract-only; full abstract and submission identity", "sectionsRead": ["abstract-only; full abstract and submission identity"], "claim": "The authors report current-direction-controlled ultrafast Néel-vector rotation in Mn2Au with optical readout.", "limitations": "Abstract-only; pulse energy, thermal controls, device yield and raw trajectories were not independently checked.", "passageKind": "research-note", "note": "The authors report current-direction-controlled ultrafast Néel-vector rotation in Mn2Au with optical readout.", "capture": "docs/field-atlas/sources/magnetism/sot.html", "sha256": "aa92ffb3dc21c3220b44d15d616125074d5ea7b