ent for reproduction?"], "title": "Zero-field deterministic all-optical writing and annihilation of nanometer-scale skyrmion bubbles", "kind": "paper", "domain": "magnetism"}</data></node><node id="mag-paper-qsl"><data key="title">2𝑘_𝐹 instability and chiral spin density wave at the 1/9 magnetization plateau in the kagome antiferromagnets</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">magnetism</data><data key="status">selected-text-review</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "mag-paper-qsl", "sourceId": "mag-src-qsl", "topicIds": ["mag-qsl"], "question": "Neural quantum-state optimization and flux insertion favor a chiral spin-density wave over previously proposed plateau states.", "method": "Selected source sections describe the reported computational/experimental method; no independent rerun.", "result": "Neural quantum-state optimization and flux insertion favor a chiral spin-density wave over previously proposed plateau states.", "whatIsNew": "Source authors’ contribution: Neural quantum-state optimization and flux insertion favor a chiral spin-density wave over previously proposed plateau states.", "limitations": "Model/ansatz/finite-size-dependent theory; not a material proof and not an independent rerun.", "status": "selected-text-review", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "Not independently replicated or computationally reproduced in this atlas pass.", "nextQuestions": ["Which independent measurement/model comparison could distinguish the principal competing explanation?", "Are the specimen geometry, disorder, uncertainty and code/data sufficient for reproduction?"], "title": "2𝑘_𝐹 instability and chiral spin density wave at the 1/9 magnetization plateau in the kagome antiferromagnets", "kind": "paper", "domain": "magnetism"}</data></node><node id="mag-paper-magnetoelectric"><data key="title">Layer dipole magnetoelectric polarizability of antiferromagnetic bilayers</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">magnetism</data><data key="status