esult": "Polarity/thickness and Cu-spacer controls distinguish spin/orbital conversion interpretations in the studied RuO2 heterostructures.", "whatIsNew": "Source authors separate spin/orbital injection signatures and use interface-spacer control to challenge a unique inverse-altermagnetic interpretation. Not a novelty certification.", "limitations": "No independent raw THz trace, calibration, supplement or transport-model fit reanalysis. The result concerns a specified specimen/channel and does not prove universal absence of magnetic order in all RuO2.", "status": "selected-text-review", "equationsUsed": [], "replication": "Not independently replicated or computationally reproduced in this atlas pass.", "nextQuestions": ["Which independent measurement/model comparison could distinguish the principal competing explanation?", "Are the specimen geometry, disorder, uncertainty and code/data sufficient for reproduction?"], "title": "[2611.09098] Disentangling Spin and Orbital Contributions in the Search for Altermagnetic Terahertz Conversion in RuO2", "kind": "paper", "domain": "magnetism"}</data></node><node id="mag-paper-moire-2026"><data key="title">[2611.31861] Superconductivity with valley-imbalanced Fermi surfaces in thick rhombohedral graphene</data><data key="kind">paper</data><data key="domain">magnetism</data><data key="status">abstract-only-review</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "mag-paper-moire-2026", "sourceId": "mag-src-moire-2026", "topicIds": ["mag-graphene"], "question": "In-plane-field-enhanced superconductivity and unequal Fermi pockets are reported in17-layer rhombohedral graphene.", "method": "Author-reported experiment/model inspected through the abstract only.", "result": "In-plane-field-enhanced superconductivity and unequal Fermi pockets are reported in17-layer rhombohedral graphene.", "whatIsNew": "Source authors’ contribution: In-plane-field-enhanced superconductivity and unequal Fermi pockets are reported in17-layer rhombohedral graphene."